Description: RTL@3D Beirut, a 3D desktop in the spirit of Sun's Looking Glass
 Windows are slabs of glass standing in a room you can turn and fly
 through, and stay working windows whatever their pose. With a 3D dock,
 a search in the header to start any app, a settings panel, and the
 Looking Glass CD viewer made into a music player and a video player. It
 installs beside the desktop you have (Ubuntu's own, or Plasma on
 Kubuntu): choose "RTL@3D" on the login screen, or make it the first
 choice there with "sudo rtl3d-login on".
 .
